<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuknoom Ch'een II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 636–c. 686</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Yuknoom the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuknoom Ch'een II, also called Yuknoom the Great, was the most powerful king of the Kaan, or snake-head, dynasty at Calakmul, ruling from 636 to about 686. He fought Tikal, controlled the rulers of cities such as Dos Pilas, Cancuen and Naranjo, and made Calakmul the leading power of the Classic Maya lowlands. Many of Calakmul's numerous stelae date from his reign and those of his successors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuknoom-cheen-ii.jpg" alt="Yuknoom Ch'een II" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard DUPONT · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Funerary_Mask_of_Yuknoom_Ch%27een_II_(Jade,_Omphacite,_Green_Quartz,_and_diverse_Shell)..._Calakmul,_Late_Classic_(600-800_AD).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
